    "summary": "Turn 12 reviewed the direct check's checker correspondence, which was the one open blocker on the violated result.\n\nWhat the check produced. The formal check for C1-recovery-adopts-committed-vector executed on the trusted runner (be74405317044c1fa5f5151c7815c026), the monitor outcome is violated with comparison_observed true, and the recorded blocker was that the direct oracle correspondence was unreviewed. The retained stream shows the sequence canonically: recovery_seed (seed lb.ballot -1, self VBallot 3), the peer's real PrepareReply delivered, peer_committed_reply (status COMMITTED, vbal 0, has_command true), then recovery_resolution with adopted_committed false, instance_status PREACCEPTED, command_after NONE and a PreAccept emitted.\n\nReview judgement. The item is checker_correspondence with status no_issue_found: the predicate (adopted_committed on the resolution event) encodes the written requirement, and the same event prints the raw stored status and the command, so the assertion is checkable against the fields rather than only through the derived boolean. Entry and caller duties are declared substitutions (recovery entered directly through startRecoveryForInstance, the peer's COMMITTED record prepared rather than produced by a proposal/commit round), which the accepted claim's scope names and which the resolution step does not depend on, since it reads only the record, the reply slice and the running ballot. Identity is shared and monotone across prerequisite and result; all handlers are synchronous, so the observation completes when the resolution returns and the emitted message code is retained. Alternatives and contrary evidence are explained in the rationale rather than hidden: the trigger substitution limits the claim to the resolution decision, and the alternative reading (the local fresh ballot legitimately outranks an older committed vbal) is recorded together with my reason for rejecting it, namely that vbal records the ballot at which a value was accepted while a fresh ballot carries none, and that the ignored reply reports the one status the protocol treats as final. Limitations keep the derived-field oracle, the harness-literal identity, and the out-of-scope consequences (accept-round completion, execution divergence) visible as independent questions.\n\nThe finding is therefore scoped and reviewable: in the declared configuration the recovering replica does not adopt a reply that reports the instance COMMITTED, and the wider consequences remain separate questions rather than part of the reviewed proposition. No map object was changed and no requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened."
